            <ArticleTitle>Iatrogenic Circumflex Artery Stenosis Following Mitral Valve Repair.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e1680</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.7759/cureus.1680</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Injury of the left circumflex coronary artery is a potentially serious complication of mitral valve surgery due to the proximity of the vessel to the posterior segment of the mitral annulus. Suture-related distortion of the artery with partial or subtotal occlusion is the most commonly implicated mechanism. Herein, we present a case of symptomatic iatrogenic circumflex coronary artery stenosis following mitral valve annuloplasty for degenerative mitral valve regurgitation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
